meta {
  name: POST charging actions update-settings (v3.0.2)
  type: http
  seq: 47
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/vehicles/{{vin}}/charging/actions/update-settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "targetSocPercentage": 80,
    "maxChargeCurrentAc": true,
    "autoUnlockPlugWhenCharged": true
  }
}

docs {
  v3.0.2 (APK audit 2026-11-18) — update charge-plan settings. Verified
  Gson wire keys of ChargeSettingsBody (com.seat.myseat.ola a60/g.java,
  @SerializedName):
    - targetSocPercentage          (int)
    - maxChargeCurrentAc           (bool, ON/OFF toggle) OR
    - maxChargeCurrentAcInAmperes  (int, explicit amperage) — send ONE, not both
    - autoUnlockPlugWhenCharged    (bool)
  null/omitted fields keep their current value (the app diffs against
  current state; b60/e0.java performRemoteUpdate). This replaces the old
  guessed shape (targetSoc_pct / maxChargeCurrentAC="MAXIMUM" /
  autoUnlockPlugWhenCharged="PERMANENT").

  Implementation: cariad/api/seat_cupra.py:command_update_charging_settings
  and command_set_target_soc (targetSocPercentage only).
  HA service: vag_connect.update_charging_settings.
}
